    {
      "id": "motion",
      "type": "inspect.scanline_motion",
      "name": "Estimate rolling-shutter motion",
      "documentation": "<p>Estimate smooth horizontal/vertical displacement versus reference row. Connect Flow and Support to Warp image with dense flow, with the current image as its Image and the reference as its Target. The field is a target-to-source pull map; the warper preserves current pixels/type/ticket and emits explicit coverage and maps.</p><p>Reference static texture must span the image height. Exclude expected moving objects with fitting selections. Forward/backward LK tracks feed a deterministic robust polynomial fit; every fourth row-sorted track is withheld for validation. Poor consensus, inadequate row support or unsafe geometry withholds Flow.</p><p>This reference-based baseline is not a physical rolling-shutter calibration or the native C++ wobble suppressor. It models row translation, not x-dependent perspective/rotation, parallax or arbitrary high-frequency vibration. Validation cannot prove rigidity or absence of defects. Retain raw captures.</p>",
      "parameters": {
        "degree": "3",
        "max_features": 800,
        "feature_quality": 0.01,
        "feature_spacing": 5.0,
        "tracking_window": 21,
        "max_pyramid_level": 3,
        "forward_backward_pixels": 0.75,
        "max_patch_error": 25.0,
        "minimum_tracks": 32,
        "minimum_training_inliers": 20,
        "minimum_inlier_ratio": 0.7,
        "inlier_pixels": 0.75,
        "fit_iterations": 10,
        "minimum_validation_tracks": 6,
        "minimum_validation_ratio": 0.8,
        "validation_pixels": 1.0,
        "minimum_row_span": 0.75,
        "maximum_row_gap": 0.25,
        "extrapolation_rows": 8,
        "maximum_motion": 32.0,
        "maximum_row_step": 2.0,
        "minimum_vertical_jacobian": 0.25,
        "maximum_work": 64000000
      },
      "position": [
        450,
        0
      ],
      "node_size": "large",
      "exposed_inputs": [
        "image",
        "reference",
        "reference_region"
      ],
      "exposed_outputs": [
        "flow",
        "support",
        "report"
      ],
      "thumbnail": true,
      "preview_output": ""
    },
