    {
      "id": "attribution",
      "type": "layout.comment",
      "name": "Original rolling-shutter fixtures - MIT",
      "description": "Original MIT coupon, video, generator and projects by OpenCVDataflowGUI contributors. No external or customer images. Known row-dependent horizontal and vertical cubic translations distort a sharp reference; independent bisection and array sampling create the captures. Native corner tracking estimates motion, separate tracks validate it, and the existing dense-flow warper corrects current pixels with explicit coverage and coordinate maps. Video has six known amplitudes at 10 fps. Moving-part fitting uses only the left static strip; the current part remains in the output. No-texture and row-gap intentionally fail without emitting a motion field. This is a row-translation baseline, not physical exposure calibration, general projective correction or defect qualification. OpenCV tracking reference: https://docs.opencv.org/5.0/main_modules/video_track.html",
      "parameters": {},
      "position": [
